I have played NetHack for about two months now.  That's right, I only
started in December '05.  I did *never* savescum or cheat in any other
way than making extensive, I mean *extensive*, or shall I say
*excessive*, use of spoilers.  I had started this human lawful Valkyrie
on Friday, the 13th of January.  And I ascended.


I continuously improved in the games I had played before, but this was
the first game where I managed to survive both Sokoban and the Gnomish
Mines.  Luck was already on my side then (as it seemed to be throughout
the entire game), as I met an ogre in the Mines who was frantically
zapping a wand of sleep at me, and managed to kill me in the process.
Turned out that the only amulet I had found so far and didn't yet manage
to identify was live saving.

After Sokoban & the Mines, things became quite a bit easier, to my own
surprise.  The break happened when I found a fully charged wand of
wishing in the Rogue level.  I took the opportunity to wish for SDSM,
CoMR, and Grayswandir (which I was curious to see), among other things.
Only after that did I attempt Fort Ludios and the Quest, both of which
weren't too much of a problem with my newly-acquired gear.

I had also found three scrolls of genocide by then.  On Dlvl 18 or 19,
a shape changer in the form of an arch-lich (I hadn't even seen a
"plain" lich before, ever!) tried to use the Touch of Death on me. (I'm
not sure whether that was before or after I wished for CoMR...)  That
was pretty scary and enough to convince me that liches are BAD.  I was
also pretty paranoid about eels and the like, so I put those scrolls to
good use.


As I saw most of the game for the very first time, I tried almost
everything once:  I took opportunity of nurses.  I did alchemy.  I tried
polypiling.  I ate rings while polymorphed into a Xorn.  I bought lots
of protection, but not until I was already XL 14 (despite my heavy
spoiler use, I didn't learn about protection until then).  As a result,
pretty much nothing after Medusa was a real threat to me anymore.

So, faster than I would have thought possible, I was in the position to
attempt my first ascension run.  I've lost count of the number of times
I was thrown back to almost the bottom of Gehennom by the "mysterious
force", but I did somehow make it out.  Again, to my surprise, nothing
spectacular happened on the Planes -- I applied the Orb of Fate each
time to find the portal and then made a run for it.  I was harassed on
the Plane of Air more than anywhere else, but I've never been in serious
danger.

On the Astral Plane, I decided to go for Pestilence first, mainly
because it was closest to my position.  Just in line with the insanely
high amount of luck I had throughout the entire game, the altar was
co-aligned, and all is well.


Unfortunately, I played this game offline.  I didn't want to play on a
public server yet due to my lack of experience -- I couldn't possibly
know that I would get _that_ far this time!  I will definitely try my
next game on a public server.


